2. Weighted Emergence Layering (WEL)
WEL is a recursive method where each emergent system output carries layered influence from prior selections:
Retained bias from previous outputs
Recurring symbolic or behavioral patterns
Salience and recency weighting
Governor-enforced continuity pressure
Example:
A generative agent in a simulated environment repeatedly selects paths that previously led to higher rewards. The AI selects actions using a drift-diffusion SDE where past high-value experiences produce a dynamic "pull" toward similar future states.
